Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Bosonic Operator Algebra", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"6d4b35a1-5eba-e261-3545-ed30b96cf6d0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This tech note introduces the symbolic bosonic algebra of the \
QuantumFramework. The ladder operators ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["a", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35b09861-2830-44c3-2166-ea2cc5ad00e8"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6aa34e1c-8bd0-3ee0-6217-faf3bf036b71"],
 " are treated as symbols obeying ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", "\[ThinSpace]", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], "]"}], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "463c6386-2b69-8d0c-1a8e-0db8954265a0"],
 ", so ordering identities, exponentials of quadratic generators and their \
matrix elements come out exact, with no Fock-space truncation. A truncation \
can enter only at the end, when a symbolic result is required as a matrix."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.004011497774788*^9, 4.0040115068548183`*^9}},
 CellID->38413307,ExpressionUUID->"08d0737f-2a48-82f5-66f1-f72f788347ab"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Install and load the QuantumFramework paclet and the second-quantization \
sub-package (skip the install step if it is already available):\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.004011511938862*^9},
 CellID->1798147401,ExpressionUUID->"0ebe674e-8808-3928-54ad-5d276f25552b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

